{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgthfxfeHrXTCDfwRQWaA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"An important correction. The index note says hidden state 24 is taken after the final norm, so my previous decomposition was invalid. Its \"layer-23 mixer\" row compared a normalized vector with an un-normalized one, and the other layers' contributions were scaled by the wrong norm (underestimated about 14-fold). The claim that layer-23 attention alone writes the copy in loops is therefore unproven, and I am retracting it. A cleaner and correctly scaled way to locate the copy is the logit lens. I will apply the real final norm to the residual after each layer and measure the copy margin (actual next token versus probability-weighted alternatives) on pre-loop text, at the loop's first cycle and in late cycles. Layer 24 gives the model's exact margin. The depth at which the late-cycle margin separates from pre-loop text shows where loop-absorbing copying is built, which will guide the search for a repair. I will redo the gen_2 generality test of the repetition direction afterwards.\n\n```python\n# Hypothesis (corrected method): logit-lens copy margin shows at which depth loop copying (late >> pre/c0) is assembled; hidden_24 is post-final-norm.\nDd5 = {}\nfor t in range(2):\n    n_ = lens5[t]; y = ids5[t, 1:n_]; T_ = n_ - 1\n    alt_ids = tk5[t, :T_]; alt_w = np.exp(tl5[t, :T_]); alt_w[alt_ids == y[:, None]] = 0; alt_w /= alt_w.sum(1, keepdims=True) + 1e-9\n    Dd5[t] = E_[y] - np.einsum('tk,tkd->td', alt_w, E_[alt_ids])\nres = []\nfor l in [12, 14, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24]:\n    Hh = np.load(f'/work/fwd_5/hidden_{l}.npy', mmap_mode='r'); acc_ = np.zeros(3)\n    for t in range(2):\n        T_ = lens5[t] - 1; X_ = np.asarray(Hh[t, :T_], np.float32)\n        Y_ = X_ if l == 24 else X_ / np.sqrt((X_**2).mean(1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6) * wf1\n        mg = (Y_ * Dd5[t]).sum(1); m0, m3 = cyc_masks(t); pre = np.zeros(T_, bool); pre[100:on5[t]-1] = True\n        acc_ += np.array([mg[pre].mean(), mg[m0].mean(), mg[m3].mean()]) / 2\n    res.append((l, *np.round(acc_, 2)))\nprint(pd.DataFrame(res, columns=['hidden', 'pre', 'cycle0', 'late']).to_string())\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":971,"cache_read_input_tokens":75231,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":971},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b4bcd242-3053-49df-a015-76e7a59477b0","uuid":"89a4e742-5f6a-46cd-8f88-5876a06d6fcc","timestamp":"2026-11-10T05:34:16.420Z","request_id":"req_011Cgthfx6u4WmPsGATnUtP4"}
